spec ww03-blind-increment: 2 sessions, 6 permutations
# WW03. Two transactions each run the blind increment SET c.n = c.n + 1 with no
# prior read. The second writer is refused (F2), so the final value is 1 after
# one commit; only a retry reaches 2. InnoDB READ COMMITTED / REPEATABLE READ and
# PostgreSQL READ COMMITTED give 2 without an error.

starting permutation: s1i s1c s2i s2c
step s1i: MATCH (c:Counter {name:'c'}) SET c.n = c.n + 1 RETURN c.n AS n
n
-
1
(1 row)
step s1c: COMMIT
step s2i: MATCH (c:Counter {name:'c'}) SET c.n = c.n + 1 RETURN c.n AS n
ERROR: serialization conflict
step s2c: COMMIT
ERROR: cypher: transaction poisoned by a prior failed Exec statement — call Rollback
final final: MATCH (c:Counter {name:'c'}) RETURN c.n AS n
n
-
1
(1 row)

